{"id": "EUVD-2026-95919", "enisaUuid": "f9e35cb4-9bf7-3d27-a78b-c1751b42aeff", "description": "MariaDB server is a community developed fork of MySQL server. From 10.6.1 until 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2, the mariadb.service unit used /run/mysqld/wsrep-new-cluster during the next service restart. A database user with FILE privilege and a secure-file-priv configuration permitting writes to /run/mysqld could create that file and inject attacker-controlled environment values into the restarted service. This issue is fixed in versions 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T17:23:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T02:02:34", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://github.com/MariaDB/server/security/advisories/GHSA-mhvc-vqcq-7vq5", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/e3d62d4e78fd4941cef3f5053e6a50d0b32d740e", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-10.11.19", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-10.6.28", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-11.4.13", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-11.8.9", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-12.3.3", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-13.0.2", "https://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-40629"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107818"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08f5ff08-dcdc-34ad-9b12-bd3c93fa2f5b", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, "product_version": "12.3.1, < 12.3.3"}, {"id": "3b5dab8a-e475-36c9-91a0-a8ac52720291", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, "product_version": "11.8.1, < 11.8.9"}, {"id": "4c4a9ba1-33f6-3f16-b8be-c9995c62313e", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, "product_version": "11.4.1, < 11.4.13"}, {"id": "55932a5c-fcdb-